---
/**
 * /security: the canonical security page. Audit facts mirror
 * docs.ophis.fi/audits exactly (inherited CoW settlement audits + the two
 * Ophis-specific pieces reviewed internally). No external audit firm is named
 * because none is engaged; do not add one here without a verifiable public
 * relationship. MEV claims keep the qualified wording from the homepage FAQ.
 */
import ContentPage from '../layouts/ContentPage.astro'
import { canonicalPage } from '../data/canonicalPages'
import { SOVEREIGN_CHAIN_LIST as sovereignList } from '../data/chains'

const { updated } = canonicalPage('/security/')

const FAQS = [
  {
    q: 'Is Ophis custodial?',
    a: `No. Ophis is non-custodial. Orders are gasless, off-chain, EIP-712-signed intents; the trader or agent signs with its own key and the keys never leave the signer. An agent signs a bounded capability with a hard limit price, not an arbitrary transaction.`,
  },
  {
    q: 'Is Ophis audited?',
    a: `The core settlement contract is CoW Protocol's audited code, so CoW's settlement audits apply to it directly. Two pieces are Ophis-specific and were reviewed in Ophis's own security audits: a hardened GPv2AllowListAuthentication with a two-step manager transfer, and the partner-fee settlement-buffer handling. Ophis has not yet engaged an external audit firm for the fork-specific pieces.`,
  },
  {
    q: 'Is MEV protection guaranteed?',
    a: `Orders settle through CoW Protocol batch auctions, which are designed to protect trades from MEV such as front-running and sandwiching by settling at a uniform clearing price. An order can never be settled below its signed limit price. Batch-auction settlement mitigates MEV by design; it is not an absolute guarantee against all adversarial conditions.`,
  },
  {
    q: 'How should an autonomous agent trade safely?',
    a: `Build a bounded order with a hard limit price, pin the receiver to the owner, and resolve the per-chain settlement domain via the @ophis/sdk helpers or the MCP list_chains tool before signing. On ${sovereignList} the settlement contract lives at a non-canonical address, so signing against CoW's canonical address yields a domain the deployed contract rejects. Set an expiry, and keep signing keys separate from custody of meaningful balances.`,
  },
  {
    q: 'How do I report a vulnerability?',
    a: `Follow the disclosure policy in SECURITY.md in the public repository. Report privately first; do not open a public issue for an exploitable finding.`,
  },
]
---

<ContentPage
  title="Security | Ophis"
  description="How Ophis handles security: non-custodial EIP-712 intents, CoW Protocol's audited settlement contracts, qualified MEV protection, agent safety rules, and vulnerability disclosure."
  path="/security/"
  heading="Security"
  lede="Non-custodial by construction: bounded, signed intents settled on CoW Protocol's audited contracts. This page is the canonical reference for the custody model, audits, and disclosure."
  updated={updated}
  faqs={FAQS}
>
  <p>
    <strong>The short version:</strong> Ophis never holds keys or funds. A trade is an off-chain
    EIP-712 order with a hard limit price, signed by your own key and settled in a CoW Protocol
    batch auction. The settlement contract is CoW's audited GPv2 code, and the fork-specific pieces
    were reviewed in Ophis's own security audits. Details and links below.
  </p>

  {FAQS.map((f) => (
    <section>
      <h2>{f.q}</h2>
      <p>{f.a}</p>
    </section>
  ))}

  <h2>Sources and links</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      Audit references and the fork delta: <a href="https://docs.ophis.fi/audits">docs.ophis.fi/audits</a>
    </li>
    <li>
      CoW Protocol's settlement contract audits:
      <a href="https://github.com/cowprotocol/contracts">github.com/cowprotocol/contracts</a>
    </li>
    <li>
      Disclosure policy:
      <a href="https://github.com/ophis-fi/ophis/blob/main/SECURITY.md">SECURITY.md</a>
    </li>
    <li>
      Agent safety in depth (receiver pinning, domain resolution, spending limits):
      <a href="https://docs.ophis.fi/ai-agents">docs.ophis.fi/ai-agents</a> and the
      <a href="https://ophis.fi/.well-known/agent-skills/ophis/SKILL.md">Ophis agent skill</a>
    </li>
    <li>
      Which chains are Ophis-operated: <a href="/supported-chains/">supported chains</a>
    </li>
  </ul>
</ContentPage>
